messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/addtiffo/addtiffo.c
Line: 95
Function: main
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: In the option-parsing loop, argv and argc are adjusted but the loop condition still evaluates argv[1][0] without verifying that at least two arguments remain. If invoked with only "-r" and no value (initial argc==2), the code does argv += 2; argc -= 2; making argc==0 and then re-evaluates while (argv[1][0] == '-'), which reads argv[1] past the end of the argv array (original argv[3]) and dereferences it, causing an out-of-bounds read/segmentation fault.

Source context:
